COMPILATION: 
    gcc main.c -o bots -lpthread

EXECUTION:
    ./bots

CLEANUP:
    make clean

Design Decisions:
  Numbered IDs were assigned and passed to each thread, making it safe to determine which threads were odd and which were even.
  Each thread was given a sleep behavior depending on its odd or even status, so threads wait periodically. The semaphore 
  FLAG was used to ensure the thread remained exclusive while accessing the shared file, preventing data corruption. pthread_join()
  is called in a separate loop after all threads are created to ensure all 7 threads run concurrently. 

Extra features:
  Each line in the QUOTE.txt file is numbered. The code keeps track of how many lines have been created in the text file.

Deficiencies:
  (Team): During our early development, we initially found it challenging to interpret the thread ID requirement and determine whether the assignment
  expected the pthread identifier or a custom thread number. After reviewing the specifications, we implemented numbered thread IDs (pthread_id() to distinguish between
  the even and odd threads for the quote selection.

Lessons Learned:
  We learned how to use semaphores to prevent conditions where multiple threads access a shared resource. We also learned how synchronization processes.
  They are essential for maintaining data integrity in multi-thread programs. 
